      "sc:author": {
        "@id": "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9347-2014"
      },
      "sc:description": "Mol Biology Tools is a free browser-based suite for sequence analysis, primer design, plasmid editing and wet-lab calculations. Its sequence tools cover PCR and Sanger primer design, primer walking plans, binding checks, screening primers against a selected DNA reference, restriction site analysis, reverse complements, ORF finding, DNA-to-protein translation and codon optimisation. Assembly PCR, Gibson assembly and site-directed mutagenesis designers support cloning design, while Plasmid Editor lets users inspect and edit supplied DNA and annotations. Calculators cover ligation, molarity, dilution, buffer preparation and multi-solute solution recipes. The tools process input sequences locally in the browser, without requiring an account or uploading those sequences to a server.",
